From e73f239d1024aa60597e7dc2acf8ba9d90022ac0 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Junction 2026 team <junction2026@localhost>
Date: Sat, 14 Nov 2026 04:05:22 -0800
Subject: [PATCH 7/9] fix(ui): recent snapshots: Space captures, unlabelled
 shown, failed edits refetched

- After a switch in the Recent list was clicked it keeps focus, inside the
  popover, where the controls' Space handling did not reach: Space flipped it
  back (a second PATCH) and captured nothing. The list now handles Space like
  the controls do: it captures, and flips or presses nothing.
- A snapshot taken before labels existed (defective null) is shown as
  "Unlabelled", with Good and Defective buttons to label it, not as good; the
  toast and describeSnapshot say "Unlabelled" for it too.
- When a label change fails, the list is fetched again, so that it shows what
  the backend has rather than what was asked for.
- Escape in a Recent comment drops the edit (it was saved on the way out).
- Recent shows times with milliseconds (and the -1 of a second snapshot in the
  same millisecond), so that two snapshots in one second are told apart.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
